stored as assets of the pre-release sources-bc-1 (pack builds read those assets, never the hosts). Licence
pages read 2026-11-11:

  CHS NONNA-10 and NONNA-100 bathymetry, Canadian Hydrographic Service, Fisheries and Oceans Canada, from the
  CHS GeoServer WCS https://nonna-geoserver.data.chs-shc.ca/geoserver/wcs (GetCapabilities: Fees NONE,
  AccessConstraints NONE), tiles picked from the indexes NONNA10.zip and NONNA100.zip of DFO catalogue
  record d3881c4c-650d-4070-bf9b-1e00aabf0a1d.
    Licence: CHS NONNA Licence, https://api-proxy.edh-cde.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/catalogue/records/d3881c4c-650d-4070-bf9b-1e00aabf0a1d/attachments/CHS_NONNA_LICENCE-LICENCE_NONNA_DU_SHC.pdf
    and the Open Government Licence – Canada, https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada
    Its clause 7 requires the CHS notice on every derived product: src/chartpack/notices/chs.txt, which the
    release notes of sources-bc-1 carry.
  BC Freshwater Atlas coastline (WHSE_BASEMAPPING.FWA_COASTLINES_SP), Province of British Columbia, from the
  WFS https://openmaps.gov.bc.ca/geo/pub/WHSE_BASEMAPPING.FWA_COASTLINES_SP/ows (Fees NONE,
  AccessConstraints NONE).
    Licence: Open Government Licence – British Columbia 2.0,
    https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/data/policy-standards/open-data/open-government-licence-bc
    Attribution: src/chartpack/notices/ogl-bc.txt, also in the release notes of sources-bc-1.

Tide station datums (regions/datum/wa-stations.toml) are from the NOAA CO-OPS datums API, a US
Government work.

Lake Union and Lake Washington polygons (regions/datum/lakes.geojson) are derived from the NOAA ENC
cells US5SEA* (M_SDAT areas, low water of the lakes), a US Government work (public domain); built by
scripts/make-lakes.py. The lakes' managed low level (regions/datum/wa-stations.toml, [[lakes]]) is
from US Army Corps of Engineers, Seattle District, publications, a US Government work (public domain).

Bundled fonts (fonts/, used to render glyph ranges):

  Noto Sans v2.015 (Regular, Bold)  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt)
    Static hinted TTFs from the notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic release NotoSans-v2.015.

Symbols (symbols/*.svg) are drawn in-house after US Chart No. 1 (public domain).
